{%- comment -%}
  THE case-study card. One component, one slot ORDER, three variants, one card-level link.
  Built 2026-07-31 (James: "for casestudies we should have a standard block across all parts of
  the website ... so the same look"). Replaces eight divergent hand-rolled copies.

  WHY IT LOOKS LIKE THIS — the rules come from published design systems, not taste:

  · The HEADING CONTAINS THE ONLY CARD-LEVEL LINK. Every system that documents a card requires a
    real heading element and puts the link inside it (NHS digital service manual, USWDS Collection,
    Nord, BBC GEL Promo, Polaris MediaCard). Our cards had NO heading at all — the title was a
    <span class="rd-cscard__inst"> — and the link text was "Read the story" on all seven impact
    cards pointing at seven destinations. WCAG 2.4.4 counts only the ENCLOSING paragraph/list-item
    as programmatically determined context, so a descriptive sibling <span> does not qualify.
    Putting the descriptive text inside the anchor fixes the failure at the root.

  · NEVER wrap the card in <a>. Five of the eight old sections did; the accessible name became the
    entire card text. BBC GEL and the NHS both reject wrapper anchors explicitly. The whole card
    still feels clickable via a stretched ::before on the heading link — the NHS/GEL/Giraudel
    pattern — which keeps one tab stop and one sensible accessible name.

  · The footer CTA is a <span>, NOT a link. It is an affordance for the heading link. A second
    anchor to the same destination is announced twice and takes a second tab stop.

  · AT MOST ONE other link — the source. It is raised (position:relative; z-index:1) above the
    stretched overlay and given real spacing so it cannot be mis-tapped.

  · Variants may HIDE slots and change scale/direction. They may NEVER reorder them. Reordering is
    exactly what made the old featured card (quote → attr → context) read as a different component
    from the old grid card (outcome → context → quote).

  · Metric chips capped at 2. No charity or B2B site surveyed puts metrics inside the card at all —
    they sit in a separate band. Keeping a couple is a deliberate BBC differentiator, but a long
    row becomes a second headline.

  · Press provenance ("as reported in …") belongs OUTSIDE the card, as a sibling of the group.
    Putting it inside either nests anchors in a card link (parser failure, hit here 2026-07-22) or
    creates the multi-link problem above.

  USAGE
    {% render 'bbc-cscard',
         variant: 'grid',                     featured | grid | compact
         kind: 'prisons',                     must match a filter value exactly
         heading: 'Sally Allsopp, HMP Lowdham Grange: "…"',
         url: '/blogs/impact/…',
         outcome: 'One line, the result.',
         context: 'Two lines of why it matters.',
         attr: 'Build to Bond · HMP Lowdham Grange',
         chips: '6 weeks × 18 hours|OCN Level 2',   pipe-separated, first 2 used
         date: '2025',
         source_label: 'the award coverage',
         source_url: '/blogs/news/…',
         image_pic: <image object>,  image: <url or asset name>,
         youtube: '…', video_file: <file>,
         cta: 'Read the story',
         anchor: 'proof'                            optional id, for deep links and #-scoped CSS
    %}
  Wrap calls in <ul class="rd-csgrid">…</ul>; this snippet renders its own <li>.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} CONTENT-AWARE SIZE (2026-08-01). The band was one shape repeated; giving cards a
   colour then exposed a second problem — a stretched card with short copy showed 50% dead
   surface. Size is therefore DERIVED from what a card actually holds, not set by position:

     has a film            → wide   a video card earns the room, and it is the strongest thing
                                    on the estate that nobody can currently see
     long copy (>150 ch)   → tall   the text needs the height rather than being cramped
     no image              → flat   nothing to reserve media space for
     otherwise             → unit

   `size` (a schema setting) overrides the derivation when an editor wants a specific card to
   lead. The grid then uses grid-auto-flow:dense so a wide card never leaves a hole beside it —
   that is the actual mechanism for "no blank spaces", not manual ordering. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign _len = context | default: '' | size -%}
{%- assign _auto = 'unit' -%}
{%- if image == blank and image_pic == blank and youtube == blank -%}{%- assign _auto = 'flat' -%}
{%- elsif youtube != blank or video_file != blank -%}{%- assign _auto = 'wide' -%}
{%- elsif _len > 150 -%}{%- assign _auto = 'tall' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign _size = size | default: _auto -%}
{%- comment -%}
  item_tag: the grid-cell wrapper. Defaults to `li` so every existing caller is untouched —
  bbc-stories-band renders these inside <ul role="list">, which is correct. But theme BLOCKS
  (blocks/bbc-case-study.liquid) render into whatever container the editor built, and on
  /pages/why-bamboo that is a bbc-group <div>. An <li> with no list parent loses its listitem
  role, which axe reports as serious (listitem x5, found 2026-08-05). The block path passes
  'div'; the card inside is already an <article>, so no semantics are lost.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign _tag = item_tag | default: 'li' -%}

{%- assign _v = variant | default: 'grid' -%}
{%- assign _cta = cta | default: 'read the story' -%}
{%- assign _kind_slug = kind | downcase | strip -%}

{%- comment -%} FAMILY (2026-08-01). An audit found 17 different `kind` values across 27 cards,
   most used once — I had invented them ad hoc while populating. Colouring by `kind` on that
   taxonomy would give seventeen colours, which is confetti, not a system.

   So the editorial label stays specific ("prisons", "expedition") and the FAMILY is derived
   here instead. Four families, four surfaces, and `data-kind` is left untouched so the existing
   conformance rule and any future filter keep working on the specific value.

   Colour has to encode something true or it is decoration: the family tells a reader what KIND
   OF PROOF a card carries before they read a word. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign _fam = 'journey' -%}
{%- assign _programme = 'prison,school,universit,delivery,famil,programme,bond' -%}
{%- assign _applied  = 'livelihood,development,enterprise,material,cargo,design' -%}
{%- assign _recog    = 'press,recognition,funder,award,coverage' -%}
{%- assign _pl = _programme | split: ',' -%}
{%- for w in _pl -%}{%- if _kind_slug contains w -%}{%- assign _fam = 'programme' -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign _al = _applied | split: ',' -%}
{%- for w in _al -%}{%- if _kind_slug contains w -%}{%- assign _fam = 'applied' -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign _rl = _recog | split: ',' -%}
{%- for w in _rl -%}{%- if _kind_slug contains w -%}{%- assign _fam = 'recognition' -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} rd-reveal sits on the <li>, not the <article>, so the WHOLE card (media included)
  fades in as one object. Restored 2026-07-31: standardising the markup dropped the class the old
  hand-rolled cards carried, which left 0 of 19 case-study cards animating on pages where 21 other
  elements did — the grids sat dead still while everything around them moved. The motion itself is
  governed by the estate's reduced-motion rules; this only opts the card into the existing system.
{%- endcomment -%}
<{{ _tag }} class="rd-cscard-item rd-reveal" data-size="{{ _size }}"{% if item_attrs %} {{ item_attrs }}{% endif %}{% if anchor != blank %} id="{{ anchor }}"{% endif %}>
  <article class="rd-cscard rd-cscard--{{ _v }}{% if youtube != blank or video_file != blank %} rd-cscard--video{% endif %}"
           data-family="{{ _fam }}"
           {% if _kind_slug != blank %}data-kind="{{ _kind_slug }}"{% endif %}>

    {%- comment -%} 1 · MEDIA — aspect-locked so a missing or odd-ratio image cannot rag the row.
       Hidden in the compact variant. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless _v == 'compact' -%}
      {%- if image_pic != blank or image != blank or youtube != blank or video_file != blank -%}
      <div class="rd-cscard__media">
        {%- if youtube != blank or video_file != blank -%}
          {%- render 'bbc-media', image: image_pic, src: image, video: video_file, youtube: youtube, alt: heading -%}
        {%- elsif image_pic != blank -%}
          <img src="{{ image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }}"
               srcset="{{ image_pic | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ image_pic | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ image_pic | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
               sizes="{% if _v == 'featured' %}(max-width: 860px) 92vw, 560px{% else %}(max-width: 749px) 92vw, (max-width: 980px) 45vw, 30vw{% endif %}"
               alt="" loading="lazy" width="{{ image_pic.width }}" height="{{ image_pic.height }}">
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if image contains '//' -%}
            <img src="{{ image }}&width=900" srcset="{{ image }}&width=480 480w, {{ image }}&width=900 900w, {{ image }}&width=1200 1200w"
                 sizes="{% if _v == 'featured' %}(max-width: 860px) 92vw, 560px{% else %}(max-width: 749px) 92vw, (max-width: 980px) 45vw, 30vw{% endif %}"
                 alt="" loading="lazy" width="900" height="563">
          {%- else -%}
            <img src="{{ image | asset_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="900" height="563">
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%} alt="" throughout: the heading immediately below carries the same meaning,
           so describing the image again is duplicate noise for a screen-reader user. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if kind != blank -%}<span class="rd-cscard__kind">{{ kind }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endunless -%}

    <div class="rd-cscard__body">

      {%- comment -%} 2 · HEADING — required, unique, and the ONLY card-level link. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        <h3 class="rd-cscard__heading">
          {%- if url != blank -%}
            <a class="rd-cscard__link" href="{{ url }}">{{ heading }}</a>
          {%- else -%}
            {{ heading }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </h3>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} 3 · OUTCOME — the countable result. Hidden when compact. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if outcome != blank and _v != 'compact' -%}<p class="rd-cscard__out">{{ outcome }}</p>{%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} 4 · CONTEXT {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if context != blank and _v != 'compact' -%}<p class="rd-cscard__ctx">{{ context }}</p>{%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} 5 · ATTRIBUTION {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if attr != blank and _v != 'compact' -%}<p class="rd-cscard__attr">{{ attr }}</p>{%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} 6 · METRIC CHIPS — max 2, see header note. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if chips != blank and _v != 'compact' -%}
        {%- assign _chips = chips | split: '|' -%}
        <ul class="rd-cscard__outs" role="list">
          {%- for c in _chips limit: 2 -%}<li>{{ c | strip }}</li>{%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} 7 · META — date · source. The only provenance inside the card, and the only
         other permitted link. Raised above the stretched overlay in CSS. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if date != blank or source_label != blank -%}
        <p class="rd-cscard__meta">
          {%- if date != blank -%}<span>{{ date }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if date != blank and source_label != blank -%}<span class="rd-cscard__dot">·</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if source_label != blank -%}
            {%- if source_url != blank -%}
              <a href="{{ source_url }}{% if source_url contains '?' %}&{% else %}?{% endif %}ref=case-study"{% if source_url contains '//' %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ source_label }}</a>
            {%- else -%}<span>{{ source_label }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} 8 · FOOTER CTA — a <span>. Never a second anchor. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if url != blank and _v != 'compact' -%}
        <p class="rd-cscard__foot"><span class="rd-cscard__more">{{ _cta }} <span class="rd-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span></p>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>
  </article>
</{{ _tag }}>
